{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:10.60.570","page_type":"section"},"citation":"10.60.570","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.60.570","content_hash":"8fc79d146f2ed75b46fd7a5fb5b081960b50e9a1b4898cc138fc4251fda444da","heading":"Grounds for adjudication by mail or administrative hearing.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.60.570:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.60.570","text":"A person charged with a parking violation may contest the charge through an adjudication by mail or at an administrative hearing limited to one or more of the following grounds with appropriate evidence to support:\n(a) That the respondent was not the owner or lessee of the cited vehicle at the time of the violation;\n(b) That the cited vehicle or its license plate was stolen at the time the violation occurred;\n(c) That the relevant signs prohibiting or restricting parking were missing or obscured;\n(d) That the relevant parking meter was inoperable or malfunctioned through no fault of the respondent;\n(e) That the facts alleged in the parking violation notice are inconsistent or do not support a finding that the specified regulation was violated; or\n(f) That the illegal condition described in the parking violation notice did not exist at the time the notice was issued. (Ord. 17636 § 6, 1-9-01. Code 1995 § 142-521.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"12aca0a2-4040-514a-83c3-7dd973c74cf7"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"10.60.570","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.60.570","content_hash":"1c80fb53fd625f02693ce108c8fa8c9d402f40053734cb497b8851cc4bd0f810","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-